{
  "bridge_text": "寒风吹拂着莉娜的红外套，那阵低沉的嗡嗡声仿佛在树干深处轻轻回应着你的好奇心。我们就顺着这片霜雪覆盖的田野，继续探寻那棵神秘大树的秘密。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "莉娜屏住呼吸，踩着咯吱作响的积雪，一步步走向那棵发出嗡嗡声的大树。树干比村里的教堂还要高大，她在树下停住脚步，指尖轻轻触碰着冰冷的树皮，心中满是对于那未完故事的渴望，终于下定决心推开了那扇仿佛一直在等待她的树门。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Perhaps that grumpy fox hides a heavy heart behind his gruff words. Let us see if Lina can find the secret he keeps tucked away in the shadows.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood her ground, her eyes bright with curiosity. The old fox, Mosk, shifted his weight, his ears twitching as if he were listening to a sound far away. He sighed, a soft rustle of dry leaves, and finally stepped aside to let her pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them and said, this is for the trouble of walking me down. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk standing firm at the top of the stairs, Lina knew she had to show him she meant no harm. She took a deep breath, ready to face whatever lay beneath the roots.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed sternly at the door, his eyes narrow and suspicious. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season, a crisp, red treasure. She set it gently on the step between them and whispered that it was for the trouble of her arrival. Mosk stared at the fruit for a long time, his grey whiskers twitching, before he finally stood up, adjusted his green vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Down in the depths of the tree, the humming revealed itself as a tired, quiet song. A firefly the size of a robin lay curled on a bed of moss, her golden glow flickering like a dying candle. Mosk’s paws trembled as he looked at her. He whispered that she had been his friend once, but long ago, he had failed to bring her medicine in time. He had been guarding this hollow ever since, trapped by the weight of his own shame."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Even with the risk of being caught, Lina felt the apple was a small price for a kinder path. With the gift placed firmly on the wood, the fox finally moved.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door, his eyes narrowed. Lina chose to offer the last apple of the season instead of sneaking away, believing that kindness might bridge the distance between them. She set the fruit on the step, and Mosk stared at it as if it were a rare treasure. He stood, adjusted his vest, and stepped aside, signaling that the path was finally open."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With the firefly resting softly upon that velvet moss, the air grew still. Her faint glow flickered, reminding Mosk of the winter he spent guarding this hollow tree in silence.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming softened into a quiet song. A firefly the size of a robin lay upon the moss—that soft, green carpet cushioning the earth like a living pillow. Her glow was fading fast. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at her. She had been his friend once, and he whispered that he had once failed to bring her medicine. He had been guarding this tree ever since, too ashamed to face her until now."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt beside the mossy bed and asked the queen what she needed. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, the queen replied; that was all medicine ever truly was. Mosk fetched the milk in a tiny thimble, laying his paw gently beside her wing. As the queen’s glow steadied, the humming inside the tree shifted into a tune Lina had never heard before, and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk the fox watching her from his perch on the stairs, Lina stood firm against his warnings. She knew that the mystery of the humming was far too important to leave behind.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a curl of stairs spiraled into the shadows. At the very top step sat Mosk, an old grey fox wearing a patched green vest. His voice sounded like dry leaves skittering across pavement as he told Lina the tree was off-limits and she should return home to forget the humming. Lina shook her head, insisting that she could not possibly forget a song she had not yet heard."
    }
