{
  "bridge_text": "While we wonder if the firefly's light will hold, the quiet music of the tree seems to wait for an answer. Let us see what happens when Lina reaches out to help.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Lina knelt beside the moss, watching the dim light pulse like a fading star. She asked the firefly queen what she needed to feel strong again. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, the queen whispered, for that was all the medicine she had ever truly required. Mosk hurried to fetch the milk in a tiny silver thimble, placing his steady paw beside her fragile wing."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "As the queen sipped, her glow began to brighten, turning the hollow tree into a sanctuary of soft gold. The humming inside the bark transformed into a melody Lina had never heard before, a song of old winters and new beginnings. For the first time in many years, Mosk hummed along, his voice shaking off the dust of his long, lonely vigil."
    }
